{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Round 2 plan-review remediation complete.\n\n- Final `3083-ada3` description length: 7,430 characters.\n- The plan now names both CE call sites that must widen their service filter: `_refresh_rates()` at `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py:184-190` and `_ce_spend_today()` at `handler.py:348-353`.\n- The exact shared service allowlist is `[\"Amazon Bedrock\", \"Claude Sonnet 4.5 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)\", \"Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)\", \"Claude Haiku 4.5 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)\", \"Claude Opus 4.7 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)\"]`.\n- `_refresh_rates()` now explicitly requires grouping by `SERVICE` and `USAGE_TYPE`, then deriving `USE1-Claude Sonnet 4.5-input-tokens` from `Claude Sonnet 4.5 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)` + `USE1-MP:USE1_InputTokenCount-Units`.\n- `_ce_spend_today()` is explicitly called out as undercounting today because its current `SERVICE == \"Amazon Bedrock\"` filter excludes Claude Marketplace services; this is now stated as an authoritative-spend defect, not silently bundled into rate loading.\n- Estimated-rate provenance was removed from this ticket and split into follow-up `conclusive-daemonic-graywolf` (`d082-5fe8-0f98-49fc`), linked back with `discovered_from`.\n- Structural checks passed: `check_ac` and `quality_check` pass for both `3083-ada3` and `d082-5fe8-0f98-49fc`.\n\nNo repository files were modified. No claim, transition, plan-review gate, completion-verification gate, `make test`, or `make verify` was run. No background process was started."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789878750595062883,"uuid":"fc3360cb-d07b-4046-a0f9-ce582414e6c1"}